Package: cohalu
Type: Package
Title: CO-localization, Hotspots And Sample-Level Units for Spatial Omics
Version: 0.99.3
Authors@R: person("Jun", "Inamo",
                  email = "juninamo@keio.jp",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: COHALU (CO-localization, Hotspots And sample-Level Units; read
    "koharu") quantifies how cell types, transcripts or other labelled
    populations are arranged relative to each other in spatial omics data. It provides a
    permutation-based neighborhood enrichment test (z-score and
    observed-over-expected effect size), radius-based co-occurrence ratios, a
    per-cell local co-localization score smoothed over the neighbor graph, and
    detection of connected interaction spots. Scores can be computed for each
    image of a multi-sample study and compared between disease groups with
    Wilcoxon, t, linear mixed model or blocked permutation tests that treat
    the biological unit (patient, donor, animal) as the unit of analysis. Seurat objects and plain
    coordinate tables are supported as input, and simulators with a planted
    cell-cell interaction are included for benchmarking.
